        <h2>Summary / Description</h2>
        <div class="description">
          The Foot Ground Interface Flight Calibration Unit (FGI FCU) is used to calibrate insoles for the Total Force Foot Ground Interface (TF-FGI) at a known air pressure.  The FGI FCU consists of two aluminum plates and a plumbing assembly.  A neoprene rubber bladder is attached to one of the plates.  
<P>
During use, the insole to be calibrated is inserted between the aluminum plates.  The FGI FCU is connected to the HRF Rack pressurized nitrogen supply via a Quick Disconnect (QD), and the metering valve is used to control the flow of nitrogen into the bladder.  A battery-powered digital pressure gauge is used to monitor the pressure exerted by the bladder on the insole.  Three relief valves are included in the plumbing assembly to prevent rupture of the bladder due to over-pressurization.  Once calibration is complete, the metering valve is closed, nitrogen from the FGI FCU bladder is vented to the cabin, the insole is removed and ready for use.
<P>
During on-orbit use the FGI FCU will be attached to the HRF Rack seat track via an ISS Multiuse Bracket.  The FGI FCU is connected to the ISS Multiuse bracket via the mounting shoe on the lower plate of the FGI FCU assembly.<END>
        </div>

